@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
allowmixing
title Proposed — Consumer expectations and provider verification
!pragma useVerticalIf on
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

rectangle "Consumer candidate\nactual used fields / outcomes / version assumptions" as C
artifact "Reviewable shared contract\nshape + semantic invariants + protected frame" as K
rectangle "Provider candidate\nreal owner implementation / actual adapters" as P
rectangle "Verification evidence\nnormal / denied / stale / duplicate / pending / unknown" as V
rectangle "Affected real integrations\nframework, persistence, serving, provider, native client" as I
C --> K : record actual expectations
P --> K : realize actual obligations
K --> V : verify same identified contract/candidates
I --> V : actual boundary evidence where applicable
V --> C : compatibility result / explicit limitations
V --> P : findings and actual disposition
note bottom of K
 Consumer-driven expectations cannot weaken source rules or privacy.
 No Pact/registry/tool or CI installation selected.
 Mock success and payload shape alone cannot establish semantic compatibility.
end note

@enduml
